{title: Camptown Races}
{artist: Stephen Foster, 1850}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, americana}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
The [G]Camptown ladies sing this song, [D]Doo-dah! [G]Doo-dah!
The Camptown racetrack's five miles long, [D]oh, doo-dah [G]day!
I came down there with my hat caved in, [D]Doo-dah! [G]Doo-dah!
I go back home with a pocket full of tin, [D]oh, doo-dah [G]day!

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Goin' to run all night! [C]Goin' to run all [G]day!
I'll bet my money on the bobtail nag, [D]somebody bet on the [G]bay
